<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>DiagnosticCatalog.Trimming</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>DiagnosticCatalog.Trimming</RootNamespace>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    This catalogue ships on the 'trimming' train, which versions independently of the foundation so it
    can follow the .NET SDK's ILLink releases without dragging anything else along. Declaring the
    train here is the whole membership (Directory.Build.targets); it is also what makes the project
    packable, what gives it an embedded SBOM, and what puts the icon on the package.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ReleaseTrain>trimming</ReleaseTrain>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Label="Package">
    <PackageId>DiagnosticCatalog.Trimming</PackageId>
    <DevelopmentDependency>false</DevelopmentDependency>
    <Title>DiagnosticCatalog.Trimming</Title>
    <Description>The .NET trimming, Native AOT and single-file warnings (ILxxxx) as strongly referenced constants, so that UnconditionalSuppressMessageAttribute takes compile-checked references instead of magic strings. Ids and categories are read from the ILLink analyzer's own DiagnosticDescriptor instances. For Blazor WebAssembly, MAUI, Native AOT and trimmable libraries. Unofficial; not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft.</Description>
    <PackageTags>roslyn;analyzers;diagnostics;unconditionalsuppressmessage;trimming;aot;nativeaot;blazor;illink;code-analysis;catalog</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Authors>Reefact</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Reefact</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Reefact/diagnostic-catalog</PackageProjectUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    A PACKAGE reference, not a project one. The foundation rides the 'lib' train and this catalogue
    rides its own, so packing against the project would stamp a dependency on a lib version that was
    never published, and every consumer's restore would fail with NU1102 on an immutable artifact
    (ADR-0007).

    Version-less, so it resolves from Directory.Packages.props — where moving every catalogue onto a
    new foundation is one deliberate edit rather than eight.

    NOT PrivateAssets="all": the foundation must reach whoever consumes this catalogue. They need
    [DiagnosticRule] resolvable to declare rules of their own, and present at run time for reflection
    over a catalogue to work (specification §16.1).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="DiagnosticCatalog" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
